    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1089">

                <pb facs="1169" n="1073" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg1073"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Eguiguren to Mr.
                            Sherman.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of Peru</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-02-17"><hi rendition="#italic">February 17,
                        1898</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I perform the duty of expressing to the
                    United States Government the sentiments of condolence and sympathy of the
                    Government of Peru, together with my own, on account of the catastrophe which
                    has befallen the war steamer <hi rendition="#italic">Maine</hi> and the loss of
                    the lives of so many citizens of the United States.</p>
                <p>Peru, which considers all the Republics of this continent as her sisters, laments
                    their misfortunes and feels them as she does her own. The grief, therefore,
                    which now afflicts the Great Republic is also ours.</p>
                <p>I reiterate, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Victor Eguiguren.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
